WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.802
Week 19: Imperfect: Background and Habit. describe how things used to be set a scene contrast past and present

2
00:00:07.802 --> 00:00:20.599
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can describe how things used to be, set a scene, contrast past and present. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:20.599 --> 00:00:28.123
Language system. Imperfect forms; habitual past; age, time, weather, description, and ongoing background.

4
00:00:28.123 --> 00:00:35.605
Sound and delivery. Maintain the three-syllable rhythm of imperfect endings and distinguish -ía from -aba.

5
00:00:35.605 --> 00:00:45.138
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:45.138 --> 00:01:12.825
Model language. Antes había menos edificios. — Before there were fewer buildings. De niña jugaba en esta plaza. — As a child I used to play in this square. Eran las ocho y llovía mucho. — It was eight o'clock and it was raining a lot. Mientras trabajábamos, escuchábamos la radio. — While we worked, we listened to the radio. La ciudad parecía más tranquila. — The city seemed calmer.

7
00:01:12.825 --> 00:01:22.979
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
